    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a bridge between abstract ideas and practical problem-solving—something I can’t ignore but also find fascinating when broken down into manageable parts. My parents, though not deeply involved in teaching it, instilled curiosity about patterns, which I’ve carried forward. It’s both intimidating and rewarding; the challenge of understanding equations mirrors how I approach philosophy or history—slowly, with patience.",
